flowchart TD
    %% RAPTOR 5-Component Boosted Distance Calculation
    
    Q[Query Vector] --> D1[Inter-Centroid Distance<br/>(d1)]
    
    Q --> D2[Query-to-Target Distance<br/>(d2)]
    
    Q --> D3[Query-to-Source Distance<br/>(d3)]
    
    Q --> D4[Intra-Cluster Penalty<br/>(d4)]
    
    Q --> D5[Cross-Cluster Penalty<br/>(d5)]
    
    %% Boosted distance formula
    D1 --> B[Boosted Distance Formula<br/>D = α₁d1 + α₂d2 + α₃d3 + β₁d4 + β₂d5]
    D2 --> B
    D3 --> B
    D4 --> B
    D5 --> B
    
    B --> R[Final Distance Score<br/>Lower = Better Match]
    
    %% Component explanations
    D1 --> E1[Raw Distance Component<br/>• Stored in hierarchical neighbors]
    
    D2 --> E2[Query Relevance Component<br/>• Computed at query time]
    
    D3 --> E3[Source Context Component<br/>• Query-to-current-cluster distance]
    
    D4 --> E4[Intra-Cluster Component<br/>• Penalty for staying in same cluster]
    
    D5 --> E5[Cross-Cluster Component<br/>• Cost of jumping between clusters]
    
    %% Coefficient explanation
    B --> C[Coefficient Strategy<br/>α₁ = 1.0, α₂ = 0.8, α₃ = 0.6<br/>β₁ = 0.2, β₂ = 0.4]
    
    %% Performance characteristics
    R --> P[Performance Benefits<br/>• Multi-probe accuracy<br/>• Balanced exploration<br/>• Avoids local minima<br/>• Query-adaptive navigation]
    
